    },
    {
      "participant": "mongo",
      "from": 735,
      "to": 791,
      "type": "database"
    }
  ],
  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Cost is per server, not per manager",
      "items": [
        "Each host costs ~25 GETs; a UCS domain costs ~11 whether it holds 10 servers or 500 (ADR-0016, Context)",
        "Hosts run in parallel under INVENTORY_REDFISH_FLEET_CONCURRENCY, shuffled so a truncated sweep never starves the same slow hosts",
        "Supported range is ~400\u20131,000 hosts per CronJob; shard beyond that (arc42 \u00a711)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "None means could not read, never zero",
      "items": [
        "A Storage 404 once wrote zeros over good data and flipped a server with a failed disk from CRITICAL to HEALTHY (ADR-0016, 'A partial read silently heals a real fault')",
        "Now a 404/403 sub-collection is None; IngestService carries the stored value forward and lists the path in Server.unread_fields",
        "A host that does not answer is skipped and the run exits 3 \u2014 PARTIAL is the normal outcome, alerting is on staleness"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Credentials stay in the CronJob",
      "items": [
        "The fleet and per-host logins come from inventory.toml and credentials.toml mounted into the CronJob pod (redfish-standalone-collector-cronjob.yaml)",
        "Unlike the manager collectors' Secret, these files are never mounted into the Route-exposed API pod (ADR-0032 \u00a76)",
        "A session is opened per BMC and deleted on exit; Basic auth would cost an LDAP round trip per GET (ADR-0016)"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
